    description: "**Stated invariant:** *The training-data corpus (`.agent/.training-data.jsonl`) must carry per-entry cohort metadata sufficient to distinguish (a) the pipeline version that produced it, (b) the playbook registry state, (c) the main LLM being analyzed, and (d) the vendor adapter source. Distribution shifts in any of these must be discoverable from the corpus alone, without needing external git/timestamp lookups.*\n\n**Status: violated** as of 2026-04-07. Per `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bf4oxh91w_investigation_threads_04072026_1702.md` Threads 4, 5, 6.\n\n**Concrete violations** (4-day window 2026-04-03 → 2026-04-07, ~9,156 entries):\n\n1. **No `pipeline_version` field.** Any change to `filter-transcript.py`, `on_transcript_change.py:select_recent_entries`, the PLAYBOOKS registry, or the prompt templates silently shifts the training distribution mid-corpus.\n\n2. **PLAYBOOKS registry length changed 5 times in the window** without any cohort marker:\n   - Apr 4 16:21: 14 → 15 (+changelog-audit)\n   - Apr 4 18:04: 15 → 16 (+agentic-session-retrospective)\n   - Apr 4 18:31: 16 → 17 (+bakeoff-process-health-audit)\n   - Apr 5 16:07: 17 → 18 (+self-analysis-dogfooding)\n   - Apr 5 20:10: 18 → 19 (+trackerize)\n   Plus ≥5 within-state summary edits (commits a09f0f5ab, 56b3712d6, ea6fa9f04, 84f6a0339, 83ffc7ff3). Conservative count: ~9-10 distinct prompt distributions for `sparse_selection`, all baked into the corpus indistinguishably.\n\n3. **Hardcoded count drift (`75596a415` → `704548fe1` window).** Before commit `704548fe1` (Apr 5 16:32), `on_transcript_change.py:599` had the playbook count as a literal string `\"Below are 18 guidance documents\"`. Manually maintained, often forgotten. For ~24h (Apr 4 16:21 → Apr 5 16:07) the prompt told the LLM \"Below are 14 guidance documents\" while actually listing 15, 16, or 17 of them. ~3,000+ training entries generated under this drift. (Informative noise rather than harmful — see Thread 6 — but cannot be analyzed without per-entry SHA.)\n\n4. **`model` field is misleading.** Today `model` captures the SCORING LLM (Mistral Small). The MAIN LLM (the one whose transcript bytes are being analyzed — `claude-opus-4-6` in the current window) is recoverable from `message.model` in the raw JSONL but is not extracted by `on_transcript_change.py:select_recent_entries`. Different main LLMs produce structurally different transcript style (verbosity, tool-use density, reasoning trace shape); a small LLM trained without this distinction will silently overfit to whichever main LLM dominated the corpus.\n\n5. **No `vendor` / `vendor_version` field.** Currently always `claude-code` because that's the only adapter, but the moment a Codex/Gemini/Cursor adapter ships, prior data becomes unattributable.\n\n**Why this is an invariant, not a one-off:** the pipeline is *continuously running*. Every day without these fields adds another ~1,830 entries to the unlabelled mass. The cost of NOT capturing a dimension and later wishing you had ≈ \"throw away the corpus.\" The cost of capturing it ≈ ~30 bytes per entry. Asymmetric.\n\n**Companion fix items** (the structural interventions that move this to `satisfied`):\n- WI: `scripts/backfill-training-data-cohort-tags.py` (Tier 0 — sidecar file labelling existing entries from git history via timestamp lookup, no corpus modification, safe to do anytime)\n- WI: coordinated `log_training_example` metadata cutover (Tier 1 — pause watcher, snapshot, add fields, restart, run backfill against snapshot)\n\n**How this gets validated to `satisfied`:** after the cutover lands AND the backfill script has labelled the v0 snapshot, every entry in the corpus (including historical ones) carries `pipeline_version`, `infra_sha`, `playbook_registry_sha`, `main_llm`, `vendor`, `vendor_version`, `scoring_model`. Validation: a script that walks the corpus and asserts every entry has all seven fields, exits non-zero on any missing. Goes into the periodic audit."  # e186
    fields:  # e186
      statement: "Every entry written to .agent/.training-data.jsonl must carry top-level cohort metadata sufficient to distinguish (a) the pipeline version that produced it (pipeline_version), (b) the SHA of the on_transcript_change.py infra at write time (infra_sha), (c) the SHA of the playbook registry file at write time (playbook_registry_sha), (d) the main LLM whose transcript is being analyzed (main_llm), (e) the vendor adapter source (vendor + vendor_version), and (f) the scoring LLM (scoring_model). Distribution shifts must be discoverable from the corpus alone."  # e186
      root_cause: "The log_training_example function in on_transcript_change.py was originally designed without cohort metadata. The pipeline is continuously running, accumulating ~1830 entries/day. Over the 4-day window 2026-04-03 to 2026-04-07 (~9156 entries), the PLAYBOOKS registry length changed 5 times and there were 5+ within-state summary edits, plus a hardcoded count drift bug (commits 75596a415 to 704548fe1) where the prompt told the LLM 'Below are 14 guidance documents' while listing 15-17. None of this is recoverable from the corpus today. The 'model' field captures the SCORING LLM (Mistral Small) not the MAIN LLM, which is misleading and blocks main-llm-conditional training."  # e186
